id: pm-graph-3a1p
title: Graph export uses quadratic item and edge scans on large trackers
description: "The pm-graph graphFromItems builder calls items.some for relationship targets and deduplicates all edges with a final filter/findIndex. Large workspaces with many relations therefore perform repeated full scans. Replace both with indexed membership and insertion-time edge keys while preserving first-edge properties, ordering, external nodes, and export shape."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T09:15:55.866Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-29T09:46:35.686Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: Real export shape and duplicate-edge semantics are unchanged; a representative multi-thousand-item export completes within a measured bound; release and packed gates pass; all evidence is linked to this item.
repro_steps: "Inspect src/index.ts graphFromItems: items.some in addRelationship; relationships.filter with all.findIndex on every edge."
expected_result: "Graph construction scales with item and edge counts, preserving the existing export contract."
actual_result: Graph construction has O(items x edges + edges squared) scans.
